    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d527-a2">

                <pb facs="1594" n="1436" sameAs="frus:frus1906p2/pg1436"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 2.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Chargé Vignaud to
                        Consul-General Mason</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Embassy</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Paris</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1906-02-15"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">February 15,
                    1906</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: By direction of the Secretary of State, I
                    have to instruct you to take charge of the archives of the Venezuelan
                    consulate-general at Paris. This is done with the consent of the French
                    Government and with the understanding that you will confine yourself simply to
                    what is stated above.</p>
                <p>Very respectfully, yours,</p>
                <closer>(Signed) <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Henry Vignaud</hi>, <hi
                            rendition="#italic">Chargé.</hi></signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Letters to the same purport sent to—</p>
                    <p>Robert P. Skinner, consul-general at Marseilles;</p>
                    <p>Dominic I. Murphy, consul at Bordeaux;</p>
                    <p>Alphonse Gaulin, consul at Havre;</p>
                    <p>Harold S. Van Buren, consul at Nice;</p>
                    <p>Louis Goldschmidt, consul at Nantes, and</p>
                    <p>John F, Jewell, consul at Fort de France.</p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
